"comparison":"Both JPMorgan and Citi executed significant business segment reorganizations in the first half of 2024 to align reporting structures with management strategies. JPMorgan combined its Corporate & Investment Bank and Commercial Banking into a single Commercial & Investment Bank segment effective in the second quarter. Similarly, Citi completed its organizational simplification in the first quarter of 2024, eliminating legacy segments and consolidating regions to establish five new reportable operating segments (Services, Markets, Banking, Wealth, and U.S. Personal Banking). Both disclosures highlight that these changes were driven by a need for simpler management structures, improved accountability, and strategic alignment, although JPM's change involved merging two wholesale segments while Citi's involved a broader restructuring of legacy franchises and regional divisions.",
