"comparison":"Both JPMorgan and Goldman Sachs disclose their reportable business segments in Item 7, but while JPMorgan explicitly details a 2024 reorganization that consolidated segments, Goldman Sachs describes a static three-segment structure (Global Banking & Markets, Asset & Wealth Management, and Platform Solutions) without mentioning a 2024 reorganization. JPMorgan's 2024 structure resulted in three reportable segments (CCB, CIB, AWM), matching Goldman's count but with different constituent businesses and naming conventions (e.g., Goldman's 'Platform Solutions' is not present in JPM's CIB/CCB/AWM structure). The comparison highlights that both firms report through three primary segments, but JPM's disclosure is defined by the active change in that year, whereas GS's is defined by stability.",
